@@ -37,0 +42,4 @@
+- Text you paste is masked as it lands. Text you type is checked when you press Enter or Send, or Alt+Shift+M. **Until then, typed text sits unmasked in the chat box, where the site's page can read it.**
+- Features of your browser, such as spell-check services and AI writing helpers, can send what you type to the browser's maker. The TDS extension cannot stop them.
+- It stops voice input and file uploads, including dropped or pasted files, and asks you first ("Allow once"), because it cannot check them.
+- After masking, a one-line message says what was hidden, as counts per kind only (for example "2 names"), and where it comes back. It is on by default. You can switch it off; your organisation can set the default and lock it. The menu also has a short tour the first time you open it.
