-With restore on, the TDS extension puts the real values back into the answer on your screen, and they become part of the site's web page. **The site's own scripts can read them on your screen, and could send them back to the site** (for example through analytics or error reports). Other browser extensions that can read the page can see them too. The site never received them in your message, and the site's stored copy of the chat holds only the placeholders.
+There are two ways to see the real values again. Each is a switch on the welcome page and in the TDS extension menu.
+
+**1. "Show real values in TDS's own panel".** The answer with the real values is shown in a panel that the TDS extension draws over the page. The site's scripts cannot read this panel. "Copy" in the panel puts the restored answer on your clipboard, only when you press it. Other apps on your computer can read your clipboard until you copy something else.
+
+**2. "Put real values into the page itself".** The TDS extension puts the real values back into the answer on your screen, and they become part of the site's web page. **The site's own scripts can read them on your screen, and could send them back to the site** (for example through analytics or error reports). Other browser extensions that can read the page can see them too. The site never received them in your message, and the site's stored copy of the chat holds only the placeholders.
