-> **Limited Use.** The TDS extension's use of the data it reads follows the Chrome Web Store User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements. The TDS extension reads the text in the chat box on claude.ai, chatgpt.com and gemini.google.com to mask personal data before you send. On claude.ai only, and only if you switch restore on, it also reads the answers shown, to show the real values again on your screen. All of it happens on your device. The TDS extension's code makes no network calls, so it never sends this data to us or to anyone else. With restore on, the real values go back into the site's page. The site's own scripts can read them on your screen, and could send them back to the site (for example through analytics or error reports). Other browser extensions that can read the page can see them too. Restore is off by default; you choose whether to switch it on. It is not sold, not used for advertising, not used to decide creditworthiness, and not read by people. The only data we receive is a bug report that you choose to e-mail us yourself.
